# Round 5 reviews (critic, Sol, code) - scores [6, 6, 7]

## critic 6
- [high] The meta goes dead after about L20. CafAc areas 3-5 are hue-rotated copies of areas 1-2 (data/cafe.json: cushion = window sprites @300, patio = counter sprites @80, rooftop = window sprites @200), so the patio gets an indoor espresso counter and pastry case tinted green. All 4 residents sit in areas 1-2 ('2 of 4 residents' in 19-residents), so about 48 stars (roughly L20-L70) buy recoloured repeats with no new cat. Score: retention at 2 months is 3/10.
  FIX: Give each area at least one new resident and its own sprite set. If that art is not ready, ship only 2 areas plus a teaser card ('Patio opens soon', with a silhouette resident) instead of the recolours.
- [high] The combo popup still sits over the LEVEL pill. In 12-purrfect, 'Meow-velous!' is drawn over the pill, and 28c shows faded combo text behind it. The comment in game.js popup() says it shows 'in the band above the conveyor', but the frames show otherwise. This was reported in round 3 and is still unfixed.
  FIX: Reserve a fixed band between the HUD row and the carriers (or draw the popup over the board's top third, under the HUD) and clamp the popup y to that band. Re-shoot 12 and 28c.
- [high] The dog wake has no visible payoff. In 24c-dog-trots-away the counter is gone, but the dog still sleeps curled in the same cell with eyes closed. Players do not see the dog react, so the mechanic reads as a counter that disappears.
  FIX: On the wake event, play an immediate beat of about 0.3 s: eyes open, a '!' or bark bubble and a stretch squash. Then play the 1.3 s trot with dust puffs. Have QA shoot the frame mid-trot.
- [medium] The tutorial text goes stale. 28c-l4-chain still says '4 of 5 seats used!' while the bench holds only 2 cats.
  FIX: Re-evaluate setTut on every bench change, and clear it once the count drops below the threshold.
- [medium] Toasts cover the Scoop booster. 'Bench: 6 seats!' and 'Bench: 5 seats!' (05, 07, 24a, 28a) and 'Pudding brought a free Scoop!' (20) sit right on the Scoop button. They appear at level start, the moment a player might tap a booster.
  FIX: Show the toast above the tutorial bar or as a pulse on the bench row, and give it pointer-events:none. Better: animate the new seat cushion popping in instead of showing text.
- [medium] On the win card, the resident's speech bubble ('You are amazing!', 'That was close!') overlaps the lives and coin pills and the LEVEL pill (zz-debug, 28d), which makes the top of the card look cluttered.
  FIX: Dim or hide the HUD while the win sheet is up, or move the bubble beside the resident inside the card frame.
- [medium] The knocked yarn rolls straight over other cats. In 25b and 06 the grey ball is drawn on top of the orange cat's head as it rolls down. The rule removes it right away (rules.js exitEffects), but the animation shows it passing through cats, which looks like clipping.
  FIX: Make the yarn hop in an arc away from the board, or draw it under the cats with a fade after one cell. Alternatively, roll it along the clear exit lane.
- [medium] The kitten link is still drawn as red or blue collar bars with a yellow dot (L12 in 05/25a, L49 in 10, L55 in 27a). It reads as a strap glitch, and the mother-kitten relation is not readable on dense boards.
  FIX: Replace the bars with a small paw-hold or tail-hook sprite between the mother's tail and the kitten's head, in the cat's own colour.
- [medium] The starter bundle opens as a modal 700 ms after entering the cafAc (main.js:182). It covers the room the player came to decorate (22-starter-offer at L11 with 80 coins). A sale during the meta reward moment hurts goodwill.
  FIX: Trigger it after the first fail/continue screen, or after a build animation finishes. Never trigger it on cafAc entry.
- [medium] The cafAc still looks like a construction site. The paint cans, roller and dust sheet stay in the foreground across every state (17, 18b, 21, 28e). The cracked plaster is still there at Counter 4/6, and Mochi sits next to the paint cans. The room never reaches cafe-a warmth.
  FIX: Move the scaffold to the next task's spot only. Shrink the crack at each build, and remove it at about 50% of the area's tasks. Give residents built-decor perches (a cushion on the window seat, the counter top) as soon as that decor exists.
- [low] The board has no surprise or variety beyond 4 modifiers. Every cat uses the same grinning sticker head, and big boards (L49, L55) turn into noise made of repeated identical heads. Score: surprise 4/10. There are no idle reactions (yawn, peek) to the player's taps.
  FIX: Add 2-3 cheap expression variants as head overlays (eyes closed, wink, 'O' mouth on the bench). Give a bonked cat a glare toward the blocker. Have a seated bench cat wave at its arriving carrier.
- [low] Cat Show is still a pure ribbon quota fed by wins (21c, 23c): it is another progress bar on top of tasks, streak and cafAc stars, with no change to gameplay.
  FIX: Use one authored Show board per theme (for example, all-yarn or frozen gauntlet) with unlimited practice and the exclusive decor as the prize.
- [low] There is a stale comment in src/main.js onWin. It says 'perk: +2 coins on every win (Mochi)', but the code adds +5.
  FIX: Update the comment.
## Sol 6
- [high] Level 3 does not force a bench decision; bench/auto-board chain not taught by hand-built level
  FIX: Hand-build Level 3 with two legal exits (off-color cat fills a cushion vs waits on bench then auto-boards). Both recoverable.
- [high] Tap destination unreadable before release (Level 12: 4 cats, 2 free seats, 3 carriers, floating orange badge)
  FIX: Show current carrier + next two slots with full pattern badges, 3 fill pips on active carrier, separate departing lane, highlight exact target on touch-down and commit on release; drop floating 4th badge.
- [high] Generated boards solvable but dull; four-colour stretches of obvious taps
  FIX: Require after tutorial at least one state with two legal exits whose post-auto-boarding consequences differ; track forced cleanup taps and reject boards dominated by them; hand-curate levels 4-10.
- [high] Share/win card shows nearly empty board and tiny static preview; bench chain is not the shareable moment
  FIX: Replay starting at setup tap with board, bench and carriers in frame; stagger cushion jumps, bigger payoff on 2nd departure, buffer next tap; 3-5s silent-readable clip on win card.
- [medium] Dog wake text says 'wakes when 3 cats leave' (global) but spec says nearby exits count; dog and yarn do not change solution
  FIX: Mark qualifying cells, tick counter only on eligible exits, dog visibly stands and clears both cells; same cause/effect for yarn; follow each teaching board with a puzzle where early use changes which carrier fills.
- [medium] Cafe has no pull beyond first room
  FIX: Mochi recurring free Hint with face on booster, tap residents where they lounge, ship playable third area, fold Cozy Room breeds in as visitors.
- [medium] Lose card (Level 49) hides bench/stranded cat behind shop-height modal and pushes paid rescue
  FIX: Freeze overflow, keep bench and active carrier visible, one-line consequence ('All 3 seats are full. Green can't board yet.'), Retry equal weight to rescue, 70-coin shortfall as secondary text.
- [low] Cat Show is a wins-to-ribbons quota with no social hook
  FIX: Weekly authored board on shared seed, unlimited practice, comparable result (peak bench occupancy), themed cafe decor reward for beating target.
## code 7
- [medium] src/game/game.js visBoard() line 620-625 clears vis.bench[e.seat] = -1 unconditionally, at time arr_C+0.44 of the tap that triggered the hop-in. visBench() (line 612) for a LATER tap can land earlier than that (arrival = t0+0.07+T, T is 0.42-0.95 s, so any second tap within about 0.5-1 s). The rules give the freed seat (lowest free index) to the new cat, so the new cat's cushion is wiped from the visual bench while rules still hold it. Chain finishes are exactly when players tap fast. Self-heals only on syncVis (undo, resize, new level); later the cat hops in from an empty cushion. Rules fuzz (tap/scoop/undo/addSeat on levels 5-120) shows rules state is consistent, so this is purely a vis-model ordering bug.
  FIX: In visBoard only clear the seat if this.vis.bench[e.seat] === e.id (and have visBench likewise skip if a pending board for that seat is still queued), or key the vis updates by cat id instead of seat index.
- [medium] src/kit/ads.js loadH5() has no timeout. h5Rewarded/h5Interstitial await it BEFORE their own START/INTER timers start. If the adsbygoogle script request stalls (captive portal, silent drop, no onload/onerror), the promise never settles, main.js guarded() leaves busy = true forever, and every guarded action (next, hint, buy, restore, adlife, adheart, share) is dead. The win card Next button then does nothing. Only reachable with VITE_ADS_PROVIDER=h5, which is the planned release config.
  FIX: Race loadH5() against a 4-5 s timer inside loadH5 itself (resolve(false) on timeout) and do not cache a timeout as a permanent failure; also make guarded() release after a max duration.
- [medium] Production gating leaves dead UI. In a default production build (ADS_CONFIG.provider 'off', AD_TEST false, iap backend fail-closed) rewarded() always returns false and purchase() always fails, yet the fail card shows 'Watch ad: +1 seat', the no-lives sheet shows 'Watch ad: +1 life', hint falls to a toast, the shop lists $ prices, and the Starter Bundle ($4.99) is shown once after L10 and then burned (shop.starterShown = true). Every one ends in 'No ad right now' / 'Purchase failed'.
  FIX: Expose ads.available() and iap.available() (provider configured or DEV) and hide or replace the ad buttons, the price tiles and the starter offer when false; do not set starterShown unless the offer was purchasable.
- [low] src/ui/ui.js settings(): cur.screen becomes 'settings' and actions.close only calls hideModal(), so ui.screen stays 'settings' after the card is gone (cafe or home keeps showing). main.js restore() (line 445) and the pwa.onChange handler (line 669) then call ui.settings() when ui.screen === 'settings'. Repro: cafe > Settings > Close > Shop > Restore, and Settings pops open over the shop. appinstalled/beforeinstallprompt fired later does the same.
  FIX: In actions.close (or ui.hideModal) restore cur to the underlying screen (cafe/home/play), or make restore/pwa check that #modal.settings really exists.
- [low] Cat Show 'exclusive decor' is sold but never delivered. Step 10 sets show.decor[themeId] = 1 and the UI shows a decor chip plus the 'A-zel dekor / Exclusive decor: <theme>' note, but econ.earnedDecor() has no caller in src/ (cafe.js and ui.cafe never render it). The player earns a reward with no visible effect.
  FIX: Render earned decor in ui.cafe (data/events.js already has a decor id per theme), or drop the chip and note until art exists.
- [low] src/main.js share() is wrapped in guarded(), so busy stays true while clip.encode runs (about 44 frames at 10 fps, 4.4 s; much longer in a background tab where setTimeout is throttled to 1/s). During that time Next (also guarded) silently does nothing. After the await the user-activation window is also gone, so navigator.share often throws and the code falls back to a file download.
  FIX: Do not hold the shared busy flag for share; use a separate 'sharing' flag, and show the PNG card immediately while the video encodes.
- [low] src/kit/clip.js tick() runs every 100 ms for the whole level and also during the win card: it allocates a new canvas and downsamples the full DPR canvas (up to 1125x2436) each time, then keeps about 48 frames (about 20 MB) alive until the next level. Pure cost on low-end phones with no gameplay benefit outside the chain moment.
  FIX: Reuse a small pool of frame canvases, stop ticking once recording is finished and the win card is up, and drop ring/best after the share or on startHome.
- [low] src/main.js adheart/hint: the reward is dropped silently when the board state changed while the ad ran (adheart returns after the ad if game.state !== st; hint skips game.setHint() if !ok()). Player watched a full rewarded ad and got nothing and no toast. Also ads.js h5Rewarded: if START_TIMEOUT fires (9 s) just before beforeAd, finish(false) is already latched while showAd() still plays, so a full view is not rewarded.
  FIX: Grant the hint/seat to the stock (or toast and refund) when the context changed; in h5Rewarded clear the start timer on the first beforeAd/beforeReward callback before any async work.
- [low] TR/EN leftovers: noAdSvg in src/ui/ui.js is a hard-coded English 'AD' text inside the 'No Ads' badge (shown on the Turkish shop and starter card); index.html has lang='en' and an English title (the runtime sets documentElement.lang but not document.title). All i18n.js keys are present in both en and tr and the placeholders match; data/cafe.json and data/events.js have tr for every name.
  FIX: Drop the text from the SVG (use a strike-through speaker/ad icon) or inject t('ad'); set document.title from t('title') on boot and on language change.

